<title>SWEDEN: Sandvik shares fall on weak 1996 result.</title>
<headline>Sandvik shares fall on weak 1996 result.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish engineer Sandvik AB fell on the Stockholm bourse on Monday after the company posted a weaker than expected profit for 1996.</p>
<p>Sandvik shares were 3.5 crowns higher before the 1996 results were released but then fell 4.5 crowns to be one crown below Friday's close at 189.5 crowns.</p>
<p>The engineering group posted a 21 percent slump in profit after financial items to 4.45 billion crowns and said 1997's profit would be about the same level.</p>
<p>The market had expected a fall of about 17 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The report was bad,&quot; said one broker. &quot;I think the share can slip further.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Jorgen Osterberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1008</p>
